/target
node_modules/
# === .handoff durability policy (ADR-0016 / ADR-0018 D1 — HFTASK-0067) ===
# The kernel owns the canonical commit-vs-ignore taxonomy. ADR-0018 D1: COMMIT all durable
# .handoff state — tasks/, decisions/, context/, hooks/, policy.toml, the rendered views
# (packets/, active.md, deliveries/), AND `.handoff/ledger.events.jsonl` (the committed
# continuity truth, the deterministic JSONL export). Only the BINARY LEDGER CACHE + ephemeral
# runtime + out-of-tree migration artifacts are ignored below — the binary ledger is re-derived
# from the JSONL via `hf import`. Never add a bare `.handoff/`/`.claude/` ignore (Git can't
# re-include past an excluded parent dir). `**` also covers the top-level path + grit worktrees.
.handoff/**/ledger.db
.handoff/**/*.db-wal
.handoff/**/*.db-shm
.handoff/**/*.rvf
.handoff/**/*.rvf.lock
.handoff/**/*.sqlite.bak
.handoff/**/*.redb.tmp
/.handoff/workspaces/

.grit
/_workspace/
/_workspace_prev/

# HFTASK-0048: the on-disk lock mirror is ephemeral advisory state (the ledger is
# authoritative); like the binary ledger cache, it is never committed.
/.handoff/locks/

# === .kb durability policy (ADR-0003 / ADR-0018 D7 — HFTASK-0072) ===
# Same text-vs-binary precedent as the .handoff ledger above (HFTASK-0067): COMMIT the
# DURABLE TEXT of the kb (`.kb/store/**` — the markdown documents + JSON commits/refs/
# manifest, the committed planning truth, analogous to `ledger.events.jsonl`) and ignore
# ONLY the BINARY DB CACHE (`.kb/.cache/gitkb.db*`, re-derived via `git kb code index`) plus
# the EPHEMERAL editing surface (`.kb/workspaces/` — checked-out copies, rebuilt from store).
# NOTE: `git kb init` wrongly ignores `.kb/store/` by default; we OVERRIDE that here so the
# durable continuity text is committed, never the churning binary. Never commit a binary DB.
.kb/.cache/
.kb/workspace/
.kb/workspaces/
.kb/config.toml
